<title>USA: Telident trims Q2 loss as sales rise.</title>
<headline>Telident trims Q2 loss as sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telident Inc cited higher expenses to support its marketing efforts Wednesday while reporting a loss of $504,357 in the second quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The company said the latest figure was lower than the $526,971 Telident lost in the second quarter of fiscal 1996.</p>
<p>The company also reported sales of $625,418, up from $437,247 one year ago.</p>
<p>Telident makes systems that track the location of a 9-1-1 emergency telephone call. Its shares closed up 1/32 at 1-15/16.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
